---
version: 2.0.2
title: parse diagnostic: keywords Pooka does not have
file: ./test/parser_error_test.gleam
test_name: missing_keyword_rendering_test
---
Source:
module main

first() {
  return 1
}

second() {
  while ready {
    work()
  }
}

third() {
  if ready { go() }
}

---
error: Pooka has no `return`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:4:3
  │
4 │   return 1
  │   ───┬──
  │      ╰─ `return` is not a keyword
  ╰─

Functions evaluate to their final expression.

help: Remove `return` and make the value the last expression of the block.

error: Pooka has no `while`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:8:3
  │
8 │   while ready {
  │   ──┬──
  │     ╰─ `while` is not a keyword
  ╰─

Repetition uses `loop`.

help: Write `loop { ... }` and leave it with `break`.

error: `if` is only used in match guards
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:14:3
   │
14 │   if ready { go() }
   │   ─┬
   │    ╰─ `if` cannot start an expression
   ╰─

Pooka has no `if` expression; conditional branching uses `match`.

help: Write `match condition { True -> ... False -> ... }`.

Found 3 errors.

